  "reproducibility_caveats": [
    "The upstream reference loader requests revision=main, so the paper does not identify an immutable dataset commit. This harness pins the current official snapshot instead of claiming a bit-identical historical snapshot.",
    "The paper specifies 512-token chunks for SH-QA, MH-QA, LME(S*) and FactConsolidation, but the current repository YAML files default to 4096. This manifest follows the paper main-experiment text.",
    "The paper says RAG settings are standardized around TopK=10, while the current official Mem0 YAML sets retrieve_num=100 and its expensive-memory methods use 4096-token chunks. Published Mem0 values are therefore contextual baselines, not a controlled common-policy retriever comparison.",
    "The published scores combine retrieval or memory construction with GPT-4o-mini answer generation. Retrieval-only diagnostics are not directly comparable.",
    "Upstream names the fourth competency Selective Forgetting in the paper and Conflict Resolution in the current README/dataset split. The underlying FactConsolidation sources are the same benchmark family."
  ]
